      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not:\n\n    var levels []ApiLevel\n    levels \u003d append(levels, finalApiLevels...)\n    levels \u003d append(levels, previewApiLevels...)\n\nIf you _really_ want to avoid the extra resize, replace the first line with:\n\n    levels :\u003d make([]ApiLevel, 0, len(finalApiLevels)+len(previewApiLevels))\n\nOr a one-liner, although a little hard to read:\n\n    levels :\u003d append(append([]ApiLevel(nil), c.FinalApiLevels()...), c.PreviewApiLevels()...)\n\nIn this case you know that c.FinalApiLevels()  returns a newly created slice that will not be passed to anyone else, so even this would be safe (assuming nobody changes the implementation of FinalApiLevels():\n\n    levels :\u003d append(c.FinalApiLevels(), c.PreviewApiLevels()...)",
